{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1397909-quiescence-and-the-spirit-arcana","id":1397909,"title":"Quiescence and the Spirit Arcana","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-21T00:46:34-07:00","id":1397909,"title":"Quiescence and the Spirit Arcana","content":"My main rp buddy and I are going to start a new Mage game, and we're excited to use Spiral from Nameless and Accursed, when it mentioned quiescence due to the tulpa she causes. Makes sense, but it reminded me that I could really use some outside opinions and advice on how to use quiescence in regards to Spirits.<br /> <br /> So, my *guess* is that Quiescence and Dissonance still work with the Spirit Spells themselves, but what about spells that Sleepers don't see, exactly? What about the Spirits themselves?<br /> <br /> Example, let's say a vengeful Mage is haunting Sleepers using Spirits. They bring a Spirit across the Gauntlet and tell the Spirit to attack someone. Can Dissonance purge the Spirit back across the Gauntlet (and would it depend on the spell?) What if you buff the Spirit to make it stronger, will a Sleeper erode the spell on the Spirit but not send the Spirit back across the Gauntlet?<br /> <br /> Or for example, I could see a Sleeper's dissonance destroying a Mage's Fetish (and not a Werewolf's) or allowing a Spirit bound to a specific location to bust free, but the Spirit continues to act as it will even as the Mage's spells break.<br /> <br /> I had a friend at one point who said that dissonance will kick in and attempt to break all spells on the Spirit, including the one used to Command the Spirit to attack a Sleeper. I know Werewolves can cause Lunacy but I don't think Spirits specifically have anything that causes Sleepers to ignore the supernatural, other than their own powers or a Sleeper's need to &quot;drink to forget&quot; cuz any breaking point is bad.<br /> <br /> I could also see it being the opposite--no dissonance on the spells if the Sleeper can't tell that the Spirit is being controlled or assisted, its just a presence or Manifested monster terrifying them, and as long as the Spirit doesn't make its spells (on it) obvious, then the Sleeper will only see what the Spirit itself is capable of doing, which is not a part of Quiescence.<br /> <br /> But I could be wrong too, or right on dissonance but not on quiescence, and that a Sleeper will forget they ever encountered the Spirit or rationalize it away *just* because a Mage was involved at some point.<br /> <br /> So what do you all think? What kinds of examples would trigger dissonance and/or quiescence with the Spirit Arcana, and which ones won't?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T02:02:32-07:00","id":1397924,"title":"","content":"I would say that only when a Sleeper is capable of percieving the effect itself as a distinct entity, that it triggers Dissonance/Quiescence. Controlling the spirit without the Sleeper being able to directly <i>perceive</i> the control (even if they <i>know</i> that the mage is controlling the spirit with a spell) will not cause Dissonance/Quiescence. Creating a new spirit with indefinite duration would trigger D/Q if the Sleeper basically thinks &quot;but this is impossible&quot; when he sees the spirit, but not if the Sleeper is clued in on the existence of supernatural and recognizes the existence of Spirits as being perfectly normal. In the latter case they would not be able to tell the difference between a normal spirit and one created by Supernal magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T02:03:15-07:00","id":1397926,"title":"","content":"I'd lean toward the spell only being affected by Dissonance if it can be perceived by the Sleeper. Otherwise it's not really obvious magic so it shouldn't be affected. Which does mean Spirit will be a really subtle arcana to operate through most of the time. I don't think that's a bad thing though since it will give Mind a run for its money that way.<br /> <br /> I'd also say Quiesence won't kick in unless it meets those criteria either, though it will almost certainly cause Breaking Point checks in most Sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T10:22:24-07:00","id":1398007,"title":"","content":"I rule that &quot;subtle&quot; is context-sensitive. Spells that modify or influence supernatural entities are subtle unless an observing Sleeper is as intimately familiar with the nature and typical behavior of an entity as a Sleeper would be with natural phenomenon like gravity or weather.<br /> <br /> So a Sleeper tribal shaman in the Amazon rain forest <i>might</i> be capable of a thought such as &quot;Why is the River Spirit attacking us? We've done nothing to offend it!&quot; But most people can't differentiate the supernatural nature of a spirit from any magic that might be effecting it.<br /> <br /> Also, Making a spirit is no different from Making a rock from the perspective of a Sleeper, because both are naturally occurring phenomenon. As long as the Sleeper doesn't watch the thing get created from nothing, it doesn't trigger Q/D. The Sleeper might have a breaking point from an encounter with a Made spririt, but it's not necessarily because of the Supernal magic involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 06-21-2020, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-21T21:03:05-07:00","id":1398115,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone so far for your responses! All that is very helpful and exciting. But I did wanna ask because of the whole, if a Sleeper sees a Spirit, their first thought is, &quot;This can't be real!!&quot; irregardless of if the Spirit got there on its own, so I wanted to get second opinions. The Spirit Arcana is my favorite one (and I think underrated x3).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T02:57:24-07:00","id":1398146,"title":"","content":"While this is quite arbitrary in practice, I would consider how direct the spell of the mage interacts with and facilitates what the Sleeper sees. A mind-controlled spirit would probably never cause Quiescence because anything it does it could theoretically do anyway. The Sleeper wants to disbelieve the spirit, but the spirit is real regardless of why it's here and thus it remains. If a Sleeper for any reason would know that a spirit would not act like this (and still remain a Sleeper instead of being a Sleepwalker), then that Sleeper might realise the impossibility of the spirit's behaviour.<br /> <br /> A spirit that is Materialised because of a spell is a whole other beast. &quot;It can't exist here!&quot; thinks the Sleeper, and the Sleeper is correct even if they have no idea it's because of a spell. Same thing with a created spirit regardless of how it shows itself. It doesn't matter if spirits are naturally occurring; the Sleeper thinks it's impossible and in this case it actually is impossible if not for the reasons the Sleeper thinks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T15:01:46-07:00","id":1398242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1397909-quiescence-and-the-spirit-arcana?p=1398146#post1398146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A spirit that is Materialised because of a spell is a whole other beast. &quot;It can't exist here!&quot; thinks the Sleeper, and the Sleeper is correct even if they have no idea it's because of a spell. Same thing with a created spirit regardless of how it shows itself. It doesn't matter if spirits are naturally occurring; the Sleeper thinks it's impossible and in this case it actually is impossible if not for the reasons the Sleeper thinks.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a good example of the sort of thing I'd been thinking about (but better designed example than I thought of) when I made this post. Yeah that's the kind of edge-case stuff I was concerned about. A good ST has to stay adaptive and keep the action moving but I wanna be as consistent as possible!<br /> <br /> Because quiescence is about Sleepers seeing the Truth and rejecting it right? The mind controlled spirit's existence is rebuked, but you can't rebuke the Spirit entirely because the only thing &quot;true&quot; about it is that its mind is under control, otherwise the Spirit is &quot;natural&quot; and in the Fallen World, a part of the Lie. But the created Spirit's existence depends on the Supernal spell that gave it life, it is more &quot;True&quot; and thus fragile this side of the Abyss. So when the Sleeper denies its existence, it can harm the spell forming the Spirit.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5973_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5973\" data-vbnamecard=\"5973\">Prometheus</a> <br /> I hope you don't mind me bothering you to, but, what do you think of this argument? Is the Sleeper perceiving the spell in this case, or &quot;only the Spirit&quot;? Should it count for dissonance?<br /> <br /> I am inclined to think Tessie is right on this point, but I would also enjoy being wrong cuz it makes things easier for me going forward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7967-scarlet-witch","name":"Scarlet Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"498"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-22T15:47:44-07:00","id":1398252,"title":"","content":"In the case of a spirit generated via Making, yeah I'd probably let Q&amp;D apply. In a very real sense the spirit is the spell itself, not a byproduct of it, since if the spell goes so does the spirit. The spirit can do things to protect itself, like operate via Reaching or from Twilight, but if it Manifests right up in a Sleeper's face it's fair game for corrosion. If you didn't want your creation to run that risk there's the slightly slower path of using magic to create the right conditions for a spirit to form, or even turning one kind of spirit into another, and I'd argue that those are probably going to be safe. The former is is Lasting even, and while the latter isn't, magic isn't operating on it in a way that's discernible to Sleepers, unless they witnessed the transformation they probably have no way to tell that this isn't the spirit it once was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-23T12:32:43-07:00","id":1398405,"title":"","content":"Yep, I basically agree with Mrmdubois on this and can't think of anything else to add.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T08:33:11-07:00","id":1398788,"title":"","content":"I wonder if you extend that argument to less shocking (to Sleepers) Made or Patterned phenomenon, like lead turned to gold or just Made gold.<br /> <br /> I'm guessing that the argument for allowing Q/D to apply to a Made spirit is based on the idea that Sleeper encounters with spirits are generally uncommon and disturbing. Spirits are as much a part of the Lie as gold.<br /> <br /> The rulebook consistently uses language like &quot;obvious manifestation of the Supernal&quot; or &quot;obvious spell&quot; when talking about Q, D, and Paradox. One way to interpret that is, &quot;The phenomenon is obvious, and also it's due to Supernal magic.&quot; The other way is &quot;The phenomenon is obviously due to Supernal magic with no more reasonable explanation.&quot;<br /> <br /> I prefer the second interpretation because it permits subtle spells with obvious effects. I allow a material difference between &quot;That's a spirit!&quot; and &quot;That guy just summoned a spirit!&quot;<br /> <br /> Basically I use the &quot;<a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/when_you_hear_hoofbeats,_think_of_horses,_not_zebras\" target=\"_blank\">think horses not zebras</a>&quot; test. If a Sleeper sees it and the &quot;horses&quot; explanation is magic, then Q, D, and Paradox apply. If the &quot;horses&quot; explanation is something that can occur naturally within the rules of the Lie, then Q, D, and Paradox do not apply.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 06-25-2020, 11:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T09:27:13-07:00","id":1398804,"title":"","content":"I use a simple two step process:<br /> Is it obviously supernatural?<br /> Is it because of the Supernal?<br /> If yes on the first question, the Abyssal shard in the Sleeper's soul determines if it's because of the Supernal.<br /> <br /> The key words are &quot;clearly, openly supernatural&quot;. (Obvious magic, p.298)<br /> It's all about the Sleeper's perception (which should not be confused with belief, that's a whole other discussion). They can be exposed to any amount of Supernal stuff but it doesn't matter as long as they don't perceive it as supernatural. But once they finally do see something they consider unquestionably impossible, they would have no idea whether that's because of the Supernal or not; and that's when the Curse has to kick in and take an active role in determining whether it's Supernal or not. I don't think the Curse is so lenient it can let a supernatural entity (that literally would not exist without a Supernal spell) slide just because it's technically possible for a regular spirit to show itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T09:58:27-07:00","id":1398812,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a whole Legacy called the Quiescent in Mage Noir. You may want to check them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}